From 2ee92210b90423270a3a1c7504a3f021dc8e461f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Advait Johari <zakethegr8@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 13:52:05 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 19/19] fix(windows): call a chrome.exe outside google's
 install chromium

Classification named every chrome.exe Google Chrome, so Chromium builds that
keep the name, like Helium, were described as Google Chrome. A chrome.exe whose
image path isn't under ...\Google\Chrome (Chrome, Beta, Dev, SxS) is now
Chromium. Its setup descriptor drives the same remote-debugging page and
labels and also accepts the Chrome page title, and the profile lookup already
prefers the install's own User Data folder. When the image path can't be read
the old classification stands.
---
 .../platform-windows/src/browser_platform.rs  | 47 ++++++++++++-------
 1 file changed, 31 insertions(+), 16 deletions(-)

diff --git a/libs/cua-driver/rust/crates/platform-windows/src/browser_platform.rs b/libs/cua-driver/rust/crates/platform-windows/src/browser_platform.rs
